#!/usr/bin/env expect
#
# drive-required-only-screens.exp — render Install's TWO checklist screens against a
#                                   given target and echo each one back verbatim, so
#                                   the caller can assert on what a human would see.
#
# WHAT THIS REACHES THAT NOTHING ELSE DOES: the `r` key's hint segment and the
# "Required install" block are SCREEN CONTENT, and both are filtered by a target-state
# rule (hub-install.sh's hi_baseline_only_actionable) rather than by anything that
# reaches a machine payload. A domain that has never been touched must appear on
# neither, on either screen, even though its whole baseline genuinely reads as
# never-installed — and the only observable form of that verdict is the absence of
# those lines from a rendered checklist.
#
# IT ONLY DUMPS, which is the deliberate opposite of every other driver beside it:
# those drive a walk to an outcome, this one renders two screens and reports what they
# said. The dump_screen mechanism and why a dump rather than a match is the right tool
# for a line that may not exist are at lib/drive-baseline-only-common.exp.
#
# THE KEY SEQUENCE:
#   1. dump the domains checklist        the `r` hint and the cross-domain block
#   2. tick the domain named in argv     by KEY, never by row number
#   3. dump its FIRST sub-selection screen   that screen's own per-domain block
# One sub-selection screen is enough: hi_pending_baseline_block renders the identical
# block on every screen its domain has (that function's own header says so), so a
# second screen would re-assert one function's output rather than a second rule.
#
# The spawn and the screen helper are shared — see lib/drive-baseline-only-common.exp
# for those and for the marker contract. --format=env is what that file spawns with,
# which suits this driver too: the checklists render on stderr and this is one pty, so
# every screen still arrives here byte-for-byte as a human would receive it.
#
# Usage: expect -f drive-required-only-screens.exp SRC TARGET INSTALL HOME PATH DOMAIN
#        with SCREEN_MARKER exported (plus the markers the shared file requires).

source [file join [file dirname [info script]] drive-baseline-only-common.exp]

set tick_domain [lindex $argv 5]

expect_screen "Which domain(s)" "domains-screen"
dump_screen domains

# By KEY, never by row number — see drive-empty-technology.exp's own note: the
# onboarding checklist offers only domains with something pending, so a row number
# depends on the target's install state, which is the variable under test here.
send "$tick_domain\r"
expect_screen "1 selected" "domain-toggled"

# THE SECOND PROMPT IS AWAITED BEFORE CONFIRMING, and it is not ceremony: the re-render
# triggered by the toggle ends in its own `> `, so an Enter sent without consuming it
# would leave that prompt in the stream and dump_screen below would match IT instead of
# the sub-selection screen — reporting the domains screen twice under two names.
expect_screen "> " "domains-prompt-after-toggle"
send "\r"

dump_screen subselection
exit 0
